  "about": "Realistic nature for the wild places (world/look/real_nature.gd): Poly Haven's scanned models (CC0, art/sourced/polyhaven_forest, kept untouched) drawn in their own PBR materials. models: id -> {file, fit (the widest it may be across, world units; 1 = a 5 ft square), grow ([least, most] times that), sink (how far into the ground it is pushed, units), lie (true: turned only about the up axis, never tipped)}. places: what is strewn over a place's map (else its region's set: regions names a set in sets, for the wild maps, those whose map theme is forest, wilderness, road or riverside), by the kind of square: low (low cover '=': one piece a square, in place of the board's own boulder or woodpile, picked from the list), woods (under the trees of '#' squares that are trees), difficult ('~'), open (walkable ground, kept off the middle of the square where feet and the selection ring are). Each kind lists [model id, how many per square on average]. A catalog prop whose `ids` entry says \"set_piece\": \"real\" is drawn as one of the models its `real` list names.",
